{"kind":"article","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AnatomyOfAGame"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How a single Swift type becomes a world the engine can run."}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Gnusto"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Anatomy of a Game"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto\/anatomyofagame"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Essentials","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline"],"anchor":"Essentials"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A Gnusto game is one type conforming to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". That one type carries everything: the rooms and things, where they start, and the rules that govern them. This article covers the model underneath — how the engine finds your declarations, how one value is both a declaration and a live reference, and how the immutable world is kept separate from the state that changes as the player plays.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Once that model is clear, the rest of Gnusto follows from it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Declarations-are-stored-properties","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Declarations are stored properties"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Rooms, things, and custom state are declared as "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"stored properties"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" of the game type:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct OperaHouse: Game {","    let foyer = Location { name(\"Foyer of the Opera House\") }","    let bar   = Location { name(\"Foyer Bar\"); dark }","    let cloak = Item { name(\"velvet cloak\"); wearable }","    @Global var disturbances = 0","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When you construct the world with ","type":"text"},{"code":"GameWorld\/init(game:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the engine’s bootstrap reflects over the game value with ","type":"text"},{"code":"Mirror","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and collects every ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Global","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". It names each entity after the property it was stored in: ","type":"text"},{"code":"foyer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" becomes ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/EntityID"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"foyer\""},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"cloak","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" becomes "},{"code":"\"cloak\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and so on. You never write these IDs by hand — the property name "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"is","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" the name."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This is why declarations must live in the type’s main body, not an extension: Swift only allows stored properties there, and the Mirror only sees stored properties. (When even the declarations need to span files or ship separately, that is what a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContent","isActive":true},{"text":" bundle is for — see ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":".)"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"One-value-two-roles","text":"One value, two roles"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A declaration and a live reference are the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"same value","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"code":["let cloak = Item { name(\"velvet cloak\"); wearable }   \/\/ the declaration","","\/\/ …later, inside a rule body:","cloak.after(.take) {","    if cloak.isWorn { … }        \/\/ the live reference — reads current state","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cloak"},{"type":"text","text":" is an "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" value. Written in the game body it "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"declares"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the cloak. Used in a rule it "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"reads and writes the live cloak’s state","type":"text"}]},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/isWorn","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/isHeld","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/name","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", and so on all consult the current turn.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This works because each ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" mints a private identity token when it is created. The token — not the struct’s contents — is the entity’s identity, and it survives copying. Two items are equal when they share a token (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/==(_:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"). Inside a turn, the token resolves to the entity’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/EntityID","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and then to its state; outside a turn there is no state to read, so a live property access traps with an explanation rather than returning a meaningless value.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"References are always compile-checked. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cloak.after(.take)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hook.holds(cloak)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"foyer.north(bar)"},{"type":"text","text":" — every one is ordinary property access, so renaming a room or deleting an item breaks the build instead of the running game."}]},{"text":"The parts of the `Game` protocol","anchor":"The-parts-of-the-Game-protocol","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" gathers a handful of members, most with defaults so a small game declares only what it needs:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"title","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"intro","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"tagline","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxScore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the banner and scoring metadata.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — geography and initial placement, as a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WorldMap","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". Read once at startup to build the initial state."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"rules","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — all game logic, as a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Rules","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" value. Defaults to empty.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"verbs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — player-typeable verbs this game adds, as "},{"code":"[SyntaxRule]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Defaults to empty. See "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AddingCustomVerbs","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"content","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — content bundles the game composes itself from, as ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContents","type":"reference"},{"text":". Defaults to empty. See ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The protocol extension also hands every game three ambient references usable as bare identifiers inside ","type":"text"},{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"rules","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" blocks:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"player"},{"type":"text","text":" — the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Player"},{"type":"text","text":", for its location, score, and inventory, and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Player\/item"},{"type":"text","text":" for the player as a thing in the world (what "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"X ME"},{"type":"text","text":" examines)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"world"},{"type":"text","text":" — the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/World"},{"type":"text","text":", for rules that apply everywhere (like daemons)."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"command","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Command"},{"type":"text","text":" currently being performed, inside a rule body."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"The `map` block","anchor":"The-map-block"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"text":" is a result-builder property that yields a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WorldMap","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — a flat list of ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/MapEntry","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" statements: exits, blocked exits, initial item placements, and the player’s start."}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var map: WorldMap {","    foyer.south(bar)                 \/\/ an exit","    foyer.north(blocked: \"Not yet.\") \/\/ a blocked exit with a refusal message","    bar.north(foyer)","","    player.starts(in: foyer)         \/\/ where the player begins","    cloak.startsWorn                 \/\/ where each thing begins","    hook.starts(in: cloakroom)","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Exits are directional and one-way: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"foyer.south(bar)"},{"type":"text","text":" does not imply "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bar.north(foyer)"},{"type":"text","text":". Declaring both is deliberate, so asymmetric maps (a chute, a one-way door) need no special case. Because "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"type":"text","text":" is a builder, you can split it across files and compose it from sub-maps — see "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/SplittingAGameAcrossFiles"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Immutable definition, mutable state","anchor":"Immutable-definition-mutable-state","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Internally, the engine keeps two things strictly apart:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"definition","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" is everything that never changes during play: names, descriptions, exits, rules, and the parser’s vocabulary. It is built once, from your declarations, at startup."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"state","type":"text"}]},{"text":" is everything that ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"does","type":"text"}]},{"text":" change: where each item is, what is lit, the score, the turn count, which things have been touched, and your ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Global","isActive":true},{"text":" values.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The entire mutable state is a single ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" value. That is a deliberate design choice: because all change funnels through one value, a turn’s mutations can be committed atomically at its end (see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"), and save\/restore becomes a serialization call rather than a feature bolted across the codebase."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When you write "},{"code":"cloak.isWorn","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"player.score += 1","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in a rule, you are reading and writing that one state value through the entity’s token — never touching the definition, and never seeing another turn’s half-finished changes."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"See also","anchor":"See-also"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GettingStarted"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Player/item":{"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"item"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Item","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto4ItemV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Player\/item","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The player as a thing in the world — what ","type":"text"},{"code":"X ME","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" resolves to, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"where per-game text and rules about the player’s own body hang:","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/player\/item","type":"topic","title":"item","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GameContent":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"GameContent","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GameContent","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContent","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A self-contained slice of a game’s world: its own rooms, items, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Global"},{"type":"text","text":" state, plus the geography, rules, and verbs that go with them."}],"title":"GameContent","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gamecontent","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Item/isHeld":{"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isHeld","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/isHeld","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"True if the player is carrying the item (including worn items)."}],"title":"isHeld","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/item\/isheld"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/EntityID":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/EntityID","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A stable, human-readable entity name derived from the Swift property label","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"at registration time (","type":"text"},{"code":"let bar = Location { … }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" → ","type":"text"},{"code":"EntityID(\"bar\")","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityID","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityID","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"EntityID","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/entityid"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Player":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Player","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/player","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The player character, available as ","type":"text"},{"code":"player","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" inside any computed property","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Game","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Player","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"Player","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Player","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/AddingCustomVerbs":{"abstract":[{"text":"Teach the parser words the built-in table doesn’t know.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AddingCustomVerbs","type":"topic","role":"article","title":"Adding Custom Verbs","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/addingcustomverbs"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Location":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/location","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A place in the world.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Location"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"Location","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Location"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Command":{"title":"Command","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Command","abstract":[{"text":"A parsed player command, available inside rule bodies as ","type":"text"},{"code":"command","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/command","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Command","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Command","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/World":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"World","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/world","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/World","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Rules that apply everywhere, declared through the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"world"},{"type":"text","text":" identifier in a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rules"},{"type":"text","text":" block:"}],"title":"World","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"World","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Rules":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/rules","type":"topic","title":"Rules","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Rules"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Rules"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Rules","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The collected rules of a game, declared in one ","type":"text"},{"code":"rules","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block. Large games","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"compose: "},{"code":"var rules: Rules { cloakRules; barRules }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/WritingRules":{"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Attach game logic to items, locations, and the world."}],"title":"Writing Rules","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/writingrules"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/MapEntry":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/MapEntry","abstract":[{"text":"One statement in a ","type":"text"},{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block: an exit, a blocked exit, an initial item","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"placement, or the player’s starting location.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MapEntry","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MapEntry","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"MapEntry","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/mapentry"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/TheTurnPipeline":{"abstract":[{"text":"What happens between the player pressing Return and the next prompt.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline","kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"article","title":"The Turn Pipeline","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/theturnpipeline"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Global":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/global","type":"topic","title":"Global","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Global","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Global","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Global","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Custom game state with the same ergonomics as built-in state:","type":"text"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","title":"Gnusto","abstract":[{"text":"A Swift engine for writing parser-driven interactive fiction — text adventures in the tradition of Zork and Infocom’s ZIL.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Item/name":{"title":"name","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/name","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The item’s display name."}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/item\/name","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"name"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GameContents":{"title":"GameContents","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContents","abstract":[{"text":"The collected content bundles a game declares, in declaration order.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gamecontents","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"GameContents"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"GameContents"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GettingStarted":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GettingStarted","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Build and run your first text adventure, one piece at a time.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"article","title":"Getting Started with Gnusto","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gettingstarted"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Game":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Game"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Game"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A complete game: declarations, geography, and rules.","type":"text"}],"title":"Game","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/game","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/ContentBundles":{"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Give a region its own declarations — its own type, and even its own package.","type":"text"}],"title":"Content Bundles","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/contentbundles"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Item/==(_:_:)":{"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"==","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"Item","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto4ItemV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Item","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto4ItemV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Two items are equal when they share the same declaration identity."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/==(_:_:)","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/item\/==(_:_:)","title":"==(_:_:)","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/WorldMap":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"WorldMap","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WorldMap","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WorldMap","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The geography and initial placements of a game, declared in one block:"}],"title":"WorldMap","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/worldmap","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Item/isWorn":{"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isWorn","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/isWorn","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"True if the player is wearing the item.","type":"text"}],"title":"isWorn","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/item\/isworn"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/SplittingAGameAcrossFiles":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/splittingagameacrossfiles","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/SplittingAGameAcrossFiles","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep a large game readable by composing its map and rules from per-region helpers."}],"title":"Splitting a Game Across Files","role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Item":{"title":"Item","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","abstract":[{"text":"A thing in the world.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/item","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Item","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Item","kind":"identifier"}]}}}